 "text": "In 1844, a message flashed by wire between Washington and Baltimore. It ran on the telegraph of Samuel Morse, a former portrait painter with little electrical training. His 1840 patent describes a register, a magnet that presses a pen onto moving paper. Short pulses of current leave dots, longer ones leave lines. Lesson, combine what you know, with a field you are new to. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
